# D3, xfx only: a provider switch that really writes, and the bytes it writes.
# The profile starts on llmux with a recorded loopback url (a credential xfx
# accepts, with no daemon behind it -- nothing here asks it anything), so the
# Gateway row is a switch rather than `Already using`. fx has no counterpart
# leaf: its Gateway row opens the gated sign-in columns (#88).
xfx: seed provider-llmux-settings.json
nomodel
wait 2.5
type /provider
key Enter
wait 1
snap open
home before
key Enter
wait 2
snap commit
home after-commit
type /provider
key Enter
wait 1
key Enter
wait 1.5
snap again
home after-again
